      <p class="small">Both options swap the Option 1 tumbler for a larger engraved YETI bottle and add Rizzi Merino socks (the same sock supplied in Tier 1, at a 100-unit rate). Totals include the $7.95 logo embroidery line used consistently across every other tier and option.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
  <div class="note t"><h4>Working item spend for 133 allocated gifts</h4>
    <p><b>$32,922.24</b> with the Kathmandu Epiq as the default jacket for both tiers. If we need to reduce the budget, using the Macpac alternative for Tier 2 brings item spend to <b>$29,867.84</b>, saving <b>$3,054.40</b> across 83 Tier 2 gifts.</p>
    <p>These are working item subtotals using Pia&rsquo;s figures plus 133 Modena bags ($1,699.74 at $12.78 each, including GST, the $80 setup fee and $50 freight). Setup charges and freight for the other items, and any tax adjustments, are still to be reconciled before a final total is agreed.</p></div>
  <p class="small"><b>Price basis:</b> Pia marked her tier prices as including GST, and her 9 October updates to the YETI 36oz bottle ($62.60), Rizzi socks ($16.83), Frame Foam Trucker cap ($16.38), Access Cap 1130 ($15.73, 50 MOQ) and Modena bag ($12.78, including its setup fee and freight) also include GST. The earlier YETI quote below is excluding GST and is kept as the earlier basis; confirm engraving inclusions before finalising. The $149 Kathmandu member price was recorded on 8 October; Kathmandu stock was unavailable at the last check. The Macpac Halo's $119.99 sale price has since been superseded by a discounted bulk quote of $102 ex GST ($112.20 incl. GST) for 83 units, down from $119. Cotton-cap supplier, member pricing and mixed-size stock still need confirmation.</p>
  <p class="small"><b>*MOQ:</b> minimum order quantities shown in Pia&rsquo;s proposal. Jacket logo embroidery has a 100-unit minimum, as does the jacket itself. Neither tier alone reaches 100 (50 and 83), so both rely on one combined order of 133 jackets. Confirm all quoted quantity conditions against the final 50 / 83 allocations. The Modena rate assumes one combined order of 133 bags for both tiers, meeting the 100-unit minimum. The 50 Tier 1 gifts exactly meet the 50-unit minimums for the Frame Foam Trucker, the Access Cap 1130 and the YETI 36oz bottle. Tier 2 has 83 cotton caps against a quoted 100-unit minimum, so ordering the 100 leaves 17 spare caps (17 &times; $8.45 = $143.65, not included in the subtotals) that can go to other hampers or recipients. Confirm a revised quote if a smaller quantity is wanted. No other MOQ overages have been added to the subtotals. Branding is to be small and tasteful.</p>
</div></div>

