  <details class="quote-detail" id="sock-quotes"><summary>Socks &middot; quantity rates and initial artwork</summary><div class="quote-body">
    <div class="tw"><table><thead><tr><th>Option / supplier</th><th>Quantity rates &middot; per pair</th><th>Timing / open details</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>Custom Branded Merino Wool Socks<br>SolosSocks</td><td>60 pairs minimum: $37.95<br>120: $29.95 &middot; 250: $24.95 &middot; 500: $22.95</td><td>Quoted delivery: 7&ndash;14 days.<br>GST, freight and branding inclusions to confirm.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Bamboo Socks<br>SolosSocks</td><td>60 pairs: $27.48<br>100: $14.61</td><td>GST, freight, branding inclusions and timing to confirm.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Bamboo Socks<br>SwankySocks</td><td>100 pairs: $14.45<br>250: $12.95</td><td>GST, freight, branding inclusions and timing to confirm.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>Further supplier quotes are still awaited. Tasteful embroidery is the requested direction;
      confirm the production method and finished cost rather than assuming every quoted sock price includes it.</p>
    <figure class="sock-concepts"><img loading="lazy" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Four initial Hybrid-Ag sock artwork options from Solos, each showing front and back">
      <figcaption>Solos&rsquo; initial Options 1&ndash;4, supplied for review. No design has been selected or approved for production.</figcaption></figure>
    <p class="small">The artwork file labels the product Merino Wool but also contains a Bamboo description.
      Confirm the material, size range and branding method with the supplier before approving the design or ordering.</p>
  </div></details>

  <details class="quote-detail" id="wine-quotes"><summary>Wine with a custom label &middot; optional fallback</summary><div class="quote-body">
    <p>Wine is being priced just in case. It has not been added to either tier as a committed inclusion.</p>
    <div class="tw"><table><thead><tr><th>Supplier</th><th>Prices recorded in the quote file</th><th>Discounts / open details</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>The Neighbours Cellar</td><td>1 bottle: $64.95<br>3 bottles: $119.90<br>&ldquo;6 or more bottles&rdquo;: $237.12, with &ldquo;3 bottles for each wine&rdquo;</td><td>Confirm the exact bundle quantity and inclusions.<br>The single-bottle price is above Nathan&rsquo;s $62 summary ceiling.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>The Wine Point</td><td>Barossa Valley Organic Grenache 2022: $62<br>Barossa Valley Single Vineyard Shiraz 2021: $58<br>Tumbarumba Reserve Chardonnay 2022: $48<br>Sparrow &amp; Vine King Valley Vermentino 2025: $48<br>Premium Victorian Pinot Noir 2024: $42</td><td>Quote file records: 2 bottles, 20% off; 6, 30% off; 12+, 50% off.<br>Confirm eligible wines and how the discount applies.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>The Neighbours Cellar options listed are Central VIC Prosecco, McLaren Vale Shiraz, VIC Reserve Pinot Noir,
      Barossa Valley Sauvignon Blanc, Hunter Valley Sparkling Brut, Moscato Fizzante and VIC Reserve Ros&eacute;.</p>
    <p class="small">Nathan&rsquo;s $39.73&ndash;$62 summary is retained above. The document&rsquo;s bundle amounts do not establish $39.73 per bottle,
      so reconcile the unit price, discounts, custom-label inclusion, GST and freight before using wine in a package total.</p>
  </div></details>
</div></div>

<section class="ops-intro" id="allocations"><h2 data-n="06">Final team allocations</h2>
  <p>Jamie&rsquo;s final workbook, received 9 October 2026. Quantities are confirmed by the team; six client notes still need sorting out.</p></section>
<div class="blk"><div class="inner">
  <div class="note t"><h4>50 Tier 1 &middot; 83 Tier 2 &middot; 133 gifts</h4>
    <p>Numeric allocations cover <b>100 client accounts</b>. The workbook contains 101 client rows, including GV Crop Protection, which has a note but no quantity entered. These final quantities replace the earlier 38 / 90 draft and drive the item-spend totals above.</p>
    <p>Some clients have more than one gift. Extra or customised gifts requested in notes are still to be agreed and are not added to the numeric totals.</p></div>
  <h3 class="sub">Client notes to resolve</h3>
